/E (A phase transition occurs  when  the system goes from one state to another, when a physical parameter, like temperature is varied. When a system is rapidly quenched from a high temperature disordered phase to a low temperature ordered one, the system does not become an ordered one instantaneously. Instead, different domains are formed which compete to select the equilibrium state. The process of gradual growth of domains with time is called domain coarsening.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
