177 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 111 0 R
/E (There is an extra complication that is not contained in the Ising model. If we represent the first liquid by up spin and the second liquid by down spin, then the equilibrium properties of this system can be modelled by the Ising model with Monte Carlo dynamics.. Now, flipping a spin in the Ising model corresponds to converting the first liquid to the second one which is not allowed or not possible. Therefore, the dynamics must conserve the amount of the first and second liquids. This causes slower growth than when the ordered parameter is non-conserved.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [5]
>>
