/Title (In the above two equations there is no noise terms , this means that there is no thermal fluctuations, so we are effectively working at T=0. A schematic Renormalization Group\(RG\) flow diagram for T is given in figure 2, showing the three RG fixed points \), Tc, infinity. Any point above Tc flows to infinity and any point below Tc flows to 0. So, the final temperature Tf is irrelevant in the scaling regime for quenches into the ordered phase)
